          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">What Causes Tooth Sensitivity?</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
            Healthy teeth have a hard outer shield of enamel covering the softer dentin underneath. When enamel wears down—due to hard brushing, night grinding, acidic drinks, or gum recession—tiny tubules in the dentin are left exposed. Cold air, ice water, or hot tea then reaches the inner nerve quickly, causing a sudden, sharp twinge.
          </p>
