        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[#F7F9FA] p-6 border border-slate-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">Signs You Should Get Sensitivity Checked</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5 text-base text-slate-700 list-disc pl-5">
            <li>Sudden stinging pain when sipping cold water, ice cream, or hot chai.</li>
            <li>Discomfort when eating sweet or sour foods like lemon or mango.</li>
            <li>Notched grooves near the gumline of canine or premolar teeth.</li>
            <li>Sensitivity focused on one specific tooth (which may signal a cavity or crack).</li>
            <li>Pain that stays even after using sensitivity toothpaste for a few weeks.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
